0..77 Comment "//! A returner\'s row may stay open through a row variable, an implicit of the"
78..158 Comment "//! kind `Row`: `log` prints through `std.io.Console.Eff` and leaves the rest of"
159..235 Comment "//! its row to its caller, so one definition is used under every row holding"
236..315 Comment "//! `std.io.Console.Eff`, the variable solved at each call by the row equation,"
316..393 Comment "//! and a handler of `std.io.Console.Eff` takes `[std.io.Console.Eff | r]` to"
394..424 Comment "//! `[r]`, forwarding the rest"
425..501 Comment "//! [Hillerström-2016-liberating_effects_rows_handlers], § 2.5 and § 3.3,"
502..535 Comment "//! T-HANDLER. What refuses is in"
536..588 Comment "//! `../../pathological/control/row-variable.gandr`."
589..592 Comment "//!"
593..609 Comment "//! - see: #2270"
610..675 Comment "//! - cites: [Hillerström-2016-liberating_effects_rows_handlers]"
676..679 Comment "//!"
680..847 Comment "//! [Hillerström-2016-liberating_effects_rows_handlers]: https://doi.org/10.1145/2976022.2976033 \"Hillerström and Lindley, Liberating Effects with Rows and Handlers\""
